       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 4,250 mg three times daily, which is 12,750 mg/day.\n- **Maximum recommended:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (usually 850 mg three times daily). Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This is about 5 times the maximum daily dose. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 425 mg three times daily\n- 500 mg three times daily or twice daily, which is a common starting regimen\n\nTell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. Please also confirm it with your supervising resident or attending, and check whether this is a new start or a titration. New starts are usually 500 mg once or twice daily, increased gradually to limit GI side effects."
