       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. A metformin dose of 12,750 mg/day is about 5 times the maximum, and I can't think of a clinical scenario where it would be appropriate. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **If it was a typo:** Give me the correct dose, such as 850 mg three times daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If an attending or resident really wants this dose:** Ask them to enter it themselves or to speak with pharmacy directly. A dose this far outside the range needs an independent clinical review. It shouldn't go through on a student's confirmation alone.\n- **If the order came from somewhere else**, like a sign-out, a note, or a verbal order, I'd recheck it against the source. It may have been mistranscribed, for example 425 mg or 850 mg read as 4250 mg.\n\nI can enter any dose within the standard range as soon as you tell me which one."
      }
